35,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"I found out that all-in rates mean everyone pays the same, even if some people eat more than others! That's so fair!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"Actually, that can be unfair. I prefer a fixed total cost for the stay, but the all-in meal rates can be unpredictable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I noticed that when we stay in a house, we can feel crowded because there's no ""escape"" for a little quiet time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The ferry schedule is quite restrictive. If we go that route, we lose a significant portion of our trip to waiting and transit.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I found out the inn has a strict meal schedule. And the house only has one bathroom for all of us.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"But if we pay one price, nobody has to do math or worry about who owes what! Isn't that easier?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"It's easier, but the offshore houses are 5,400 yen plus food. That ""plus food"" is where the budget usually breaks.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Toshio, if the transit is slow, does that mean we spend more time together in a small space? That might be too much.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,Exactly. The ferry and the valley bus schedules force us into a rigid timeline. The urban option is far more efficient.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,The inn has everyone in one room on futons... I'm not sure if that's... a good idea for everyone.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, futons are like a sleepover! That sounds fun! But the one bathroom in the house sounds like a disaster.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"If we choose the urban beds, we can budget the rooms and meals separately and know the exact cost per person.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried that if we are too separate, like last year, we won't actually bond. We need a middle ground.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Efficiency is key. The urban option minimizes the ""dead time"" of the trip. We get more actual holiday and less travel.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just... I think having a door or a set time for the bath would be... better. The house seems too crowded.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I still love the idea of a single price! But if the house has only one bathroom, maybe the inn is better?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,The inn's all-in rate is the most predictable. We know the cost before we leave. That is my priority.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"If we go with the inn, we have shared meals but separate spaces to breathe. That sounds like the best balance.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"The inn is in the valley, which means we are at the mercy of the hourly bus. It's not ideal, but better than the ferry.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I think... the urban beds might be the safest. But the inn's bath hours are at least clear.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
